
P ⇔ A ∧ O ∧ E

• P (Proven Authenticity): denotes stable, formally verified epistemic certainty
of digital entity status within standardized verification frameworks, rather than
ultimate ontological truth.
• A (Artist Attestation): realizes creative subject authentication and source
right confirmation;
• O (Object Identification): establishes unique physical entity binding and
exclusive physical-digital correspondence;
• E (Evidence Certification): provides forensically robust, traceable, and
tamper-proof evidence solidification.
